    "text": "Consider a helium <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>He</mi></mfenced></math> atom that absorbs a photon of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>330</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>. The change in the velocity (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>He</mi></math> atom after the photon absorption is ______ .<br />(Assume: Momentum is conserved when photon is absorbed.<br />Use: Planck constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>, Avocados number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>He</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
  },
